    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "Media handoff",
      "pos": [
        40,
        730
      ],
      "size": [
        490,
        410
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Choose a video and soundtrack, then queue. Four MP4s show distinct audio policies.\n\nPreserve: the original VIDEO goes directly to Save Video.\nReplace: source frames/FPS plus only the supplied AUDIO.\nMix: mean of source and supplied AUDIO (built-in AudioMerge).\nLoop: repeat supplied AUDIO to the exact video duration, retaining sample rate and channels. Choose pad for a silent tail, or trim to leave short audio unchanged.\n\nSave Video trims audio longer than the video. Short replacement tracks end early. Audio to Video Duration fills the loop branch to the video duration using its rational frame rate; loops have a hard join, without crossfade.\n\nAll rebuilt branches take FPS, bit depth and color space from the source. H3 source audio is normally stereo. You may connect Generate Video or a restoration VIDEO instead of Load Video; Generate Music AUDIO may replace Load Audio. Each remote generation node keeps its own service URL/model.\n\nSee docs/media-handoff.md for supported ComfyUI revision and validation."
      ]
    },
